{"title":"Name","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Name","subtitle":"| Position, institution\n| pronouns\n| (name pronounciation)\n","about":{"template":"solana","image":"portrait_pic.jpg","image-width":"10em","image-shape":"round","links":[{"icon":"envelope","text":"Email","href":"mailto:email"},{"icon":"mortarboard-fill","text":"Google Scholar","href":"https://scholar.google.com"},{"icon":"github","text":"Github","href":"https://github.com"},{"icon":"linkedin","text":"Linkedin","href":"https://www.linkedin.com"},{"icon":"person-vcard-fill","text":"ORCID","href":"https://orcid.org/"}]}},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nThis is a template for a grad student or postdoc personal website built using quarto. I'm hopeful that it will be helpful for grad students at all levels, including those seeking industry positions, however as a postdoc I am more familiar with academic pages.\n\nBefore using this template, consider learning about quarto websites here: <https://quarto.org/docs/websites>.\n\nThis page uses the about page template, see details here: <https://quarto.org/docs/websites/website-about.html>. This page can be used to give an overview of yourself, and you can link [externally](https://quarto.org/docs/websites) and [internally](teaching.qmd).\n\nThis template uses the `zephyr` theme, to change the theme or create a custom theme go to the `_quarto.yml` file. See [here](https://quarto.org/docs/output-formats/html-themes.html) for more details about themes and see [here](https://bootswatch.com/) for a previous of what the pre-made themes generally look like.\n\nA straightforward way to publish a website is via github pages, see here for a guide on publishing a quarto website via github pages: <https://quarto.org/docs/publishing/github-pages.html>.\n\nThis goal of this template is to provide several types of pages that might be relevant, but most personal websites don't have all of these pages!\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\nThis is a template for a grad student or postdoc personal website built using quarto. I'm hopeful that it will be helpful for grad students at all levels, including those seeking industry positions, however as a postdoc I am more familiar with academic pages.\n\nBefore using this template, consider learning about quarto websites here: <https://quarto.org/docs/websites>.\n\nThis page uses the about page template, see details here: <https://quarto.org/docs/websites/website-about.html>. This page can be used to give an overview of yourself, and you can link [externally](https://quarto.org/docs/websites) and [internally](teaching.qmd).\n\nThis template uses the `zephyr` theme, to change the theme or create a custom theme go to the `_quarto.yml` file. See [here](https://quarto.org/docs/output-formats/html-themes.html) for more details about themes and see [here](https://bootswatch.com/) for a previous of what the pre-made themes generally look like.\n\nA straightforward way to publish a website is via github pages, see here for a guide on publishing a quarto website via github pages: <https://quarto.org/docs/publishing/github-pages.html>.\n\nThis goal of this template is to provide several types of pages that might be relevant, but most personal websites don't have all of these pages!\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-ove